EXT. HOT-AIR BALLOON BASKET - 400 FEET UP - DAY

A wicker box. A burner. A county fair shrunk to a quilt far below.

GLORIA PENDERGAST (60s, sun visor, clipboard) stands at one wall. Beside her, WINNIE OKONKWO-HART (20s, borrowed sweater, white knuckles on the rope).

Gloria cups her hands and bellows over the side.

                    GLORIA
          Welcome, everyone! Enjoy the view!

Nobody below hears. A cow looks up.

                    WINNIE
          Why are we shouting?

                    GLORIA
          Tradition.

Winnie closes her eyes. The basket tilts. She opens them.

                    WINNIE
                    (to herself)
          Don't look down. Don't look down.

Gloria taps her clipboard, squints at a dial, and mutters.

                    GLORIA
                    (to herself)
          Pilot never said it'd do that.

                    WINNIE
          Do what?

                    GLORIA
          Nothing. Everybody smile for the camera!

There is no camera. Winnie slowly forces a smile anyway. Gloria hands her the clipboard.

                    GLORIA (CONT'D)
          Hold this. And whatever you do, don't let go of her.

                    WINNIE
          Of who?

Gloria points at the burner. It hisses.
